   "source": "fr_agencies",
   "summary": "The Federal Register agency list covers bodies that submit documents for publication in the Federal Register. It retains defunct agencies as first-class entries and carries no active/abolished flag, so the absence of an agency is ambiguous and its presence does not imply it still exists."
